From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DREAM <dream@invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:51:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DRM access units (ETSI ES 201 980) with frame size limits

New input fields: drm_mode (create time), drm_frame_bytes / drm_frame_bytes_min (read
by every ixheaace_process() call). In DRM mode (AOT 2/5/29, 960-sample frames, one
SCE/CPE) each call returns one access unit:

- aac_crc_bits (CRC-8 x^8+x^4+x^3+x^2+1, preset 0xFF, inverted) over the element up to
  and including tns_data(), as aac_scalable_main_element() of the main layer;
- ER AAC syntax with aacSectionDataResilienceFlag = 1 (5-bit codebooks, VCB11: every
  ESC sfb a section of its own without length) and aacSpectralDataResilienceFlag = 1
  (HCR, ISO/IEC 14496-3 8.5.3.3: presorting, priority codewords, sets of non-priority
  codewords with alternating direction; short windows unit-interleaved), no RVLC;
- SBR (and MPEG-4 PS, ES 201 980 5.4.3) in DRM form: 8-bit SBR CRC instead of the
  extension type, bs_coupling bit in the SCE, no alignment, header in every AU, stored
  bit-reversed from the last bit of the AU;
- zero padding between AAC and SBR data up to the requested size.

The quantisation loop accounts the DRM side information exactly (static bits, VCB11
section bits, CRC and SBR as ancillary bits). drm_frame_bytes caps the AU (bit
reservoir included), drm_frame_bytes_min pads it and spends bits that would only be
padding on a finer quantisation; the reservoir follows the transmitted sizes and starts
empty, so a transmitter can keep every audio super frame exact while frames lend each
other bits. The library ID becomes "IXHEAACE+DRM". New files ixheaace_drm.[ch] were
written for DREAM from the standards.
